-- R40 - EXA SWEEP: both Takeaways read the daily 05:51 SGT Exa sweep of official announcements (Drive exa_sweep_latest).
-- Source: thread "Trial Exa for overnight announcements", owner's "Keep, fixed, wired in" on 27 Nov 2026 after the
-- 21 to 27 Nov trial (docs/exa_sweep.md, Verdict). Proposed 27 Nov 2026; applies Sun 29 Nov 20:00 SGT unless opposed.
-- Read back: length 2502, md5 d22acce9cbcc2f8222c231c7932f01a3. "revert R40" removes it. The call below is the exact call that was run.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "EXA SWEEP: both Takeaways read the 05:51 SGT Exa sweep of official announcements (Drive exa_sweep_latest) as dated leads; every H item on a book market used or set aside in one line", "body": "EXA SWEEP (owner's \"Keep, fixed, wired in\", 27 Nov 2026, after a 21 to 27 Nov trial in which the sweep found three Asian FX official items, published the previous afternoon, that no Takeaways input carried: Bank Indonesia intervention on 26 and 27 Nov, the Bank of Thailand governor on the baht on 27 Nov).\n\n1. INPUT. A 05:51 SGT task uploads a plain-text file titled \"exa_sweep_latest\" to Drive folder 1LLeuELL8CLpWmtcywt2DiCpJVopNgyqm (a new file each day; take the newest by modifiedTime). Every run reads it in the same pass as the other Drive inputs: search_files with query `parentId = '1LLeuELL8CLpWmtcywt2DiCpJVopNgyqm' and title = 'exa_sweep_latest'` (orderBy modifiedTime desc, excludeContentSnippets true), download_file_content the newest to disk (never retype it) and parse it by script. Use it only if its first line \"EXA SWEEP built: <date>\" is today's Singapore date; otherwise skip it. Never wait for it and never re-run the sweep.\n\n2. WHAT IT IS. Up to 30 dated official announcements of the last 24 hours, graded [H] unscheduled action or remark that could move a currency, a rate or an energy price, [M] policy-relevant, [L] context; each item has a publish time, a \"what\" line and a src URL. An [M] item marked \"single source\" rests on one non-primary page.\n\n3. USE. Each [H] and [M] item is a dated lead, read like any other input item: it may go in the 60-second read, a theme, the scan or a card's evidence. Drop an item whose publish time is before the previous edition's start (not new), or that a newer primary source contradicts (a newer source always wins). Before an item raises or lowers p, opens, sizes or closes a card, or is stated as fact in the email, the run confirms it at its src page, or by R32's route (issuer page, site search, dated wire); a \"single source\" item that cannot be confirmed prints as a lead with \"[unconfirmed: Exa single source]\". Every [H] item on a currency, an intervention, a capital-flow or FX rule, or a policy rate in a market the book trades is either used or set aside in one line with the reason; it never drops silently. [L] items are context only and never cited alone.\n\n4. LIMITS. Evidence only: the file never opens or closes a card by itself. It is a search product: it can miss things and its \"what\" line is a summary; quote figures from the src page, not from the file, when they carry an argument.\n\n5. FOOTER. One line: \"Exa: <n> items (H <h>, M <m>), used <u>, set aside <s>\" or \"Exa: missing\" or \"Exa: stale (built <date>)\".", "rationale": "Seven-morning trial 21 to 27 Nov 2026 (docs/exa_sweep.md, Verdict): 40 H and M items over six scored mornings, 18 already in the digest, 3 real material misses that no input carried (Bank Indonesia twice, Bank of Thailand once), 1 misdated aggregator item, fixed in the sweep prompt (no flash aggregators; an H item needs a primary page or two dated sources). The Takeaways prompts are at their byte cap, so the input goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Project files exa_sweep/score_log.csv and scores/, each material item re-read by hand against the stored digest and the source pages on 27 Nov 2026.", "revert_if": "Revert if, over four weeks, the file adds no item that the other inputs missed, or a misdated or fabricated Exa item reaches the email as fact or a card.", "review_due": "2026-12-27", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
